        "original_id": "b763afbc-155b-5096-98e0-6dae9e114b9a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Fire & Rescue NSW\n- Events: Granville Train Disaster, Newcastle earthquake, Thredbo landslide, major structural collapse incidents\n- Places: New South Wales, Australia\n\nFacts:\n- In 1977, the Granville Train Disaster was a large-scale collapse and the worst rail disaster in Australian history.\n- In 1977, the Granville Train Disaster caused 84 deaths, injured more than 210 people, and affected 1,300 people.\n- In 1989, the Newcastle earthquake was an earlier large-scale collapse event in New South Wales.\n- In 1997, the Thredbo landslide was an earlier large-scale collapse event in New South Wales.\n- After these earlier large-scale collapses, Fire & Rescue NSW was legislated as the combat authority for responding to major structural collapse incidents in New South Wales.",
